# loom-server environment file.
#
# Install to /etc/loom/loom-server.env.
# Every variable below is optional: with none of them set the server binds
# 127.0.0.1:38886 and keeps its log in process memory. The values below are the
# recommended production setup.
#
# There is no UI path to configure. The product app is compiled into the binary,
# so LOOM_UI_DIR — the variable this file used to point at a bundle on disk — is
# simply not read any more; a line left over from that shape is inert and the
# server serves the client it was built with.
#
# systemd reads this file literally (no shell); `KEY=value`, `#` comments, and
# quotes around values with spaces.

# --- listen address -----------------------------------------------------
# host:port. Loopback is the default and the recommended value. Do NOT put a
# public interface here: the API has no authentication and can drive command
# execution on every enrolled machine. Expose it through Tailscale, or through a
# reverse proxy that terminates TLS and authentication, and keep this on
# loopback. See docs/remote-access.md.
LOOM_BIND=127.0.0.1:38886

# --- relay log (choose exactly one) -------------------------------------
# Durable local log: one append-only file per shard under this directory. The
# replay window survives a server restart. Comment this out if you set
# LOOM_REDIS_URL; setting both is a startup error.
LOOM_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/loom/server
# Shared log in Redis Streams. Uncomment for a restart-transparent upgrade
# window shared by more than one node. See docs/redis-backend.md.
#LOOM_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# --- identity -----------------------------------------------------------
# Stamped on every envelope this node produces, so it must be unique per node.
LOOM_NODE_ID=loom-server

# --- UI (development only) ----------------------------------------------
# The product app is compiled into the binary, so a deployed server serves it
# with nothing configured here. This overrides it with a frontend dev server to
# reverse-proxy to, so the app can be edited with hot reload against a real
# server: it is the Vite dev server of a checkout
# (`pnpm --filter @bb/app run dev`), never a deployed shape.
#LOOM_UI_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# --- primary host -------------------------------------------------------
# Only for a single-machine deployment: the id of the host running on the
# server's own machine, so primary-host queries prefer it while its worker is
# attached. Leave unset for a server-only deployment; primary-host resolution
# then falls to connected remote hosts, and answers "no_host" when none exists.
#LOOM_LOCAL_HOST_ID=host_01M...

# --- local worker (single box) ------------------------------------------
# Uncomment to have this server start and supervise one `loom worker` child on
# this machine, so one unit runs both roles. The child is a separate process:
# the server restarts it when it exits and stops it when the server stops. Leave
# this off for a server-only deployment, and leave it off on a server that has a
# loom-worker@ unit of its own — that would enroll the same machine twice.
#LOOM_LOCAL_WORKER=1
# Name the child shows in the host list. Default: loom-local.
#LOOM_LOCAL_WORKER_NAME=loom-local
# URL the child dials. Default: the port of LOOM_BIND, on loopback when the bind
# is the unspecified address and on the bound address when it is not.
#LOOM_LOCAL_WORKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:38886

# --- worker self-update artifacts ---------------------------------------
# Where this server hosts the worker artifact that matches its own protocol,
# served on GET /install/loom-worker for a worker whose protocol does not match.
# See docs/upgrades.md.
#
# Unset (the default) is the directory holding this executable, which is where
# deploy/install.sh puts the matching `loom-worker` — a symlink to the same
# `loom` file the server is — so an ordinary install hosts its own artifact with
# nothing to configure here. Set it when that name is not beside the server's
# executable, or to host `loom-worker-<triple>` files for machines of another
# architecture. A containerised server runs `loom` with no such name beside it
# and so hosts nothing unless this is set.
#LOOM_ARTIFACT_DIR=/usr/local/bin
